Shared memory resources cause => race conditions

To avoid race conditions:
1) Atomic variables - some operations provided sync 
2) Synchronized - monitor => methos sync 
3) Synchronized -lock => Object sync , Sync(this)
       Sync implements Reentrant lock 
       Same thread can acquire lock many times 


Excessive Sync :
   => One thread at a time
   => Worse than single thread 
   => Multiple thread , no concurrent / parallel processing 
        => More context switching ===> More resource wastage 
  
Use Sync less ==> To get more multithread benefit 

Operations that are no atomic and in heap 
that might cause Race Condt ? Use Sync 

All reference assignment=>  Atomic
Getters,Setters - atomic 
Primitive types (except Long,Double) - atomic  
Long , Double -  64 bits long
   1 write - lower 32 bits 
   1 write - upper 32 bits 
   2 operation involved => non -atomic 

Volatile =>
Tackle issues with cache coherence 
Can be applied to Long,Double to behave atomically 
Helpful to update data where multiple theadwith different cache access 
    Makes the updated value visible to other threads 
Volatile data => Processors flush immediately 
Volatile Gurantees , shared data to be same for muti thread 
Happens-Before memory ordering :
    All the changes done by Thread A needs to be visible to thread B before accessing volatile data A , by this all prev changes before volatile data also piggyback and visible to Thread B .
    


Multithreading needs :
Mutual exlusivity -> Sync locks 
Visibility of shared resources -> volatile 

Race condt -> concurrent  executions on non atomic shared operations 
      Avoid by Atomic/Locks/sync 
Data race -> out of order executions when multiple thread access same operations 
      Avoid by  Happens before semantics 
        sync/locks - only 1 thread at a time 
        volatile - multi thread and avoid data race 

