Locking mechanism :
Coarse Grained -> Less work , might lead to single thread 
Fine Grained -> Multiple locks, more work , better parallelism 
                    might lead to DeadLock 

DeadLock :
When to thread wait for each other to release a lock
Conditions for DeadLock :
Mutual Exclusion 
Hold and Wait - atleast 1 thread is holding the resource and waiting for otherresource 
Non Preemptive Allocation - Resource released only after thread is done using it 
Circular wait - chain of at least two threads each one holding one 
Solution :
Avoid circlar wait 
Order of accessing locks must be the same 
Use Watchdog to detect deadlock 
